# Shell scripts run on Linux. Git autocrlf turned a committed .sh into
# CRLF, which made the shebang "#!/bin/bash" and produced the maximally
# unhelpful error "setsid: failed to execute: No such file or directory".
# The LF-will-be-replaced-by-CRLF warnings were the actual warning.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
